00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Hi. In this video, we'll look at using Burp Suite to test for directory traversal vulnerabilities.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,100
Directory traversal vulnerabilities, which you may also hear being called path vulnerabilities,

3
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:23,660
allow an attacker to read arbitrary files on the server running an application. This

4
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:29,680
might include application code and data, credentials for back-end systems, and sensitive operating

5
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:36,360
system files. You can use Burp Scanner in Burp Suite Professional to automatically flag potential

6
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:42,120
directory traversal vulnerabilities. You can also use Burp Intruder to insert a list of

7
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:47,920
directory traversal fuzz strings into a request. The strings may enable you to read arbitrary

8
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:54,100
files on the server. We'll be using the file path traversal traversal sequences stripped

9
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:59,120
with superfluous URL decode lab from our Web Security Academy if you'd like to follow along

10
